ries  or three they say this is really not  that consequential  and we leave it as is yeah you're right  of course this is a sign of the process  working and i hope people take that  message away  you worry that they won't however and so  i'm concerned and i wonder if you share  that concern that this could slow down  the rate of vaccination in this country  and thereby slow  slow down our return to normalcy  well i certainly hope that's not the  case and we know that about 180 million  doses of pfizer and moderna have been  administered  and not one of these cases has been seen  so certainly  americans should feel reassured that at  least with those vaccines that are  readily available now  that there should not be any incidents  we haven't seen any of this particular  rare condition  and hopefully we will get to the bottom  of what's going on with johnson and  johnson soon but  we really do need people to take the  vaccines if they can the ones that are  available that we know are safe and  effective  yeah but people are even now more  nervous tara i know you get that too but  i've got a viewer question here she  asked  i got the johnson johnson vaccine what  should i be looking for  in terms if what should i be looking for  if i have a blood clot  good question great question so if the  vaccine was administered over a month  ago the risk of this condition is  extremely rare and probably  not really an issue if the person  received the vaccine within the previous  three weeks we know that the  median day of onset of this condition  occurred about nine days  then certainly they should be looking  for things like headache a headache  that's severe and persistent  abdominal pain nausea vomiting leg pain  or swelling or shortness of breath or  chest pain do you know why women that  should prompt them to call their doctor  do you know about why women are affected  and is there a certain ethnic  we don't know that but um certainly when  you look at what's happened in europe  with the astrazeneca we also saw  predominance of women  we will need to evaluate these cases  more to figure out is there some  underlying condition that predisposed  these women that we don't know about  we know that there were cases in men  in europe with that astrazeneca vaccine  so there may be more cases that come out  here in fact  dr shuket yesterday after the press  conference mentioned that there was one  man  in the j j trial that now and  retrospectively may have had a similar  situation so it may be genetics and  hormones playing into it as well  all right tara thank you very much of  course we'll all stay on top of this  as i know you will too thanks a lot

